{
    "background_story": "Janiyah was a bright and ambitious high school student who had always been drawn to the world of science and technology. Despite facing self-doubt and imposter syndrome, she found solace in affirmations that her parents and teachers would repeat to her. 'You are capable and strong,' they would say. 'Your ideas matter and can change the world.' Janiyah began to internalize these affirmations, repeating them to herself daily. As she did, she noticed a shift in her confidence and mindset. She started to see herself as a leader and innovator, rather than just a student. With renewed faith in herself, Janiyah created a mobile app that helped underprivileged students access educational resources. Her project earned her recognition at a national science fair, and she became a role model for young girls everywhere. Janiyah's story shows the power of affirmations in unlocking one's potential and achieving greatness.",
